for r in j['routes']:
 z=r['estimator']['last'];lines.append(f"| {r['route']} | {manifest['routes'][r['route']]['count']} | {r['active_seconds']/60:.2f} | {r['qualified']['seconds']/60:.2f} | {z['factor']:.4f} | {z['offset']:.4f} | {z['friction']:.4f} |")
lines+=['','Startup values are factor 1.877481, offset 0, friction 0.209698, mapping `[0,4096] → [0,4096]`, and configured delay 0.1 s. End-of-route learned values are runtime estimator outputs, not recommended fixed tuning values. All routes report branch `sp-honda-dev-202608`, commit `c04f890f684445f57c8a7cbd3f2e7f77def80397`. carParamsSP includes an Odyssey neural-network model descriptor; this alone does not prove that its feedforward option was enabled.','', '## Status and limitations','', f"Moving temporary steering-fault flags total {sum(r['temporary_moving_seconds'] for r in j['routes']):.2f} seconds; moving permanent-fault flags total {sum(r['permanent_moving_seconds'] for r in j['routes']):.2f} seconds. Raw EPS status counts are preserved in torque_metrics.json. These status flags are not a diagnostic trouble-code scan.", '', 'Tracking uses logged desiredLateralAccel minus actualLateralAccel, not the generic controller error field: extensions may transform that field into another control domain. The logged actual acceleration is a model-derived estimate, not an independent physical torque measurement. Eligibility requires fresh valid control/carState messages, active assistance for at least two seconds, valid CAN, speed ≥10 m/s, no driver steering override, and no temporary/permanent steering fault. Sample intervals above 50 ms are excluded. Means and percentages are time-weighted; percentiles are sample-weighted. Excluded interventions and faults are reported separately, not treated as successful tracking.', '', 'Earlier PID reports use steering-angle error in degrees. These torque-controller acceleration errors must not be numerically compared to those angle errors as evidence of improvement. Route dates with stale July wall clocks are left unidentified; route 05 is the October 1 long drive and route 10 is the October 3 long drive.', '', 'The logs now support evaluation of estimator adaptation and steering tracking, but not validation of a 2.5× physical torque modification. No firmware or controller settings were changed. Further tuning decisions should account for matched speed/curvature conditions and the continuing variation in learned parameters.', '', '![Tracking and calibration](torque_tracking.png)','', 'Detailed per-speed-bin metrics, estimator ranges, EPS status counts and route durations: torque_metrics.json. Parsing metadata: each route’s .parse.json. Integrity: collection_manifest.json.']
